INT. PAWNSHOP BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Glass cases. Guitars on hooks. A TV with the sound off.

A MAN IN A GREY HOODIE (30s) tears open a drawer, dumps it. Jewelry rattles onto the floor.

Behind him, the door creaks.

SHOPKEEPER MARCUS OYELARAN-BRIGHT (50s, cardigan, baseball bat) steps in. The man turns.

MAN
Whoa. Whoa.

MARCUS
Put it down.

MAN
It's not what it looks like.

MARCUS
It looks like robbery.

MAN
Okay, it's what it looks like.

He bolts. Marcus swings. The bat clips a guitar; strings twang. They crash together against the counter, hands on each other's collars. A glass case shatters under them.

MAN (CONT'D)
(grunting)
Let go!

MARCUS
You let go!

They stagger, breathing hard. A second figure appears in the doorway.

DETECTIVE IRENE KOWALCZYK-DIOP (40s, badge on her belt, gun drawn) stands with her feet planted.

DETECTIVE KOWALCZYK-DIOP
Police. Hands.

Both men freeze. Both raise their hands. Marcus drops the bat. The man drops the loot.

MARCUS
Detective. He's the thief.

MAN
He's the owner!

DETECTIVE KOWALCZYK-DIOP
Sir. Mr. Oyelaran-Bright. I'm familiar.

She holsters, steps forward, and cuffs the man.

KOWALCZYK-DIOP
You've been busy, Danny.

DANNY
(sighing)
Hi, Irene.

MARCUS
You know him?

KOWALCZYK-DIOP
He's my brother.

A beat. Marcus picks up the bat, sets it on the counter, and quietly pours himself a drink.
